lay which served in the Indonesian Navy since 1962. Launched in 1952, and since her decommissioning in 1990 has been preserved as a monument. The body/hull was slightly cut for stairs & door for easier public entrance & viewing. Beside the monument there is a building where a short film about the history of the submarine can be viewed. You also can see the Suroboyo mon","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Surabaya","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Submarine_Monument_Surabaya_2.JPG/1280px-Submarine_Monument_Surabaya_2.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Submarine_Monument_Surabaya_2.JPG/500px-Submarine_Monument_Surabaya_2.JPG","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Midori","license":"CC BY 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Submarine_Monument_Surabaya_2.JPG"}},{"id":"surabaya_red_bridge_surabaya","areaId":"surabaya","name":"Red Bridge, Surabaya","category":"landmark","tags":["views","photo","sunset"],"location":{"lat":-7.23675,"lng":112.73837},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"surabaya_red_bridge_surabaya","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":9,"commonsNearby":34,"wikiPageviews":314,"wikidataSitelinks":3,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["redbridgesurabaya","surabaya"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"This red bridge plays a big role in Surabaya's history; not for the bridge itself, but for the Dutch colonial era commercial area which lies in northern part of the city surrounding this bridge. The area is also known as Old Surabaya. See one of the best preserved Dutch colonial quarters in Indonesia.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Surabaya","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Red_Bridge%2C_Surabaya%2C_2025_%2802%29.jpg/1280px-Red_Bridge%2C_Surabaya%2C_2025_%2802%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Red_Bridge%2